WEBVTT

00:00:10.181 --> 00:00:14.113
<v><b>Ida:</b></v> And for me, personally, I, I grew up, sort of, all over the world,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.562
we moved to a different country every three years of my life.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:29.007
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> Yeah, yeah, no, I agree. I mean, for me, I’ve got, I’ve got a young son

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:34.448
who’s about to start school, er, later this year and so we’ve had to try and choose a school for him.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.871
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> And then there was one school in particular that really stood out

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:44.776
and one of the reasons was because,

00:00:45.175 --> 00:00:49.045
not only do they have lots of different languages, cultures, backgrounds…

00:00:54.577 --> 00:00:58.301
<v><b>Ida:</b></v> That reminds me of an experience I had in school in first grade when I was living in Uruguay,…

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.115
<v><b>Ida:</b></v> …and it’s just really important, and I think it just – I then become very aware,

00:01:08.155 --> 00:01:13.440
when I am in a place that is…not that, and it makes me slightly uncomfortable,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.740
sort of, I don’t know…